  "ai_language_tip": "Open in Bahasa Melayu or English (both normal in KL/Penang); switch to Mandarin or Cantonese for Chinese-run shops and Tamil for Indian-run shops if staff do; Manglish code-mixing is normal.",
  "english_ok": "yes — English is widely used in business, hotels and private clinics in cities; less so at small Malay kampung shops, government counters and rural east coast.",
  "politeness": "Warm and indirect: open with 'Selamat pagi/petang' or 'Hello, good afternoon', use Encik/Puan/Cik, Mr/Ms or 'boss/auntie' only if they do; thank with 'terima kasih'.",
  "name_tip": "Malay names use 'bin/binti' + father's name, not a surname: use 'Encik/Puan' + given name; Chinese names surname first ('Mr Tan'); Indian names often given name + father's name.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 01X-123 4567 (10 digits) or 011-1234 5678 (11 digits); KL landline 03-1234 5678; read back in groups; WhatsApp number is usually the same mobile.",
  "time_tip": "Malay 'pukul 7.30 malam' uses a dot; 'setengah lapan' = 7:30 in Malay; English 12-hour with am/pm dominates; always read back with pagi/petang/malam or am/pm.",
  "number_tip": "Read numbers in Malay or English singly; Manglish 'double 3' for 33 is common; prices in RM with sen; Chinese-speakers may avoid saying '4' — just read digits plainly.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch rush 12:00–14:00 and dinner 19:00–21:00 at eateries, Friday 12:30–14:30 (Jumaat prayer) at Malay-run businesses, and calls after 21:00; mind Ramadan iftar time.",
  "closed_days": "Weekend is Sat–Sun except Kedah, Kelantan, Terengganu (Fri–Sat); many hawkers and Chinese eateries close one weekday; Hari Raya and Chinese New Year close shops for days.",
  "booking_channels": "WhatsApp is the default for restaurants, salons, clinics and tradesmen; TABLEAPP/Eatigo for dining, BookDoc/DoctorOnCall for doctors, Fresha for salons, Grab for rides.",
  "voice_menu": "Telcos (Maxis, CelcomDigi, U Mobile), banks, TNB electricity and Pos Malaysia use IVR with BM/English/Chinese options; small shops answer by hand or not at all.",
  "callback_habits": "Most businesses confirm or reply by WhatsApp message rather than calling back; clinics and garages may send a WhatsApp reminder the day before.",
